h+='<section class="gp-sec" id="closing"><h2>Contract to closing &amp; compliance</h2><p class="gp-note">Once a contract is signed, submit the Contract to Closing form and DA so the Managing Broker can review the file and release commission.</p><div class="gp-two">'+'<div class="gp-box"><h3>Contract to Closing + DA</h3><p>One form per contract (Rev 11-2026): transaction, parties, title company or attorney, commission, referral and disbursement. Start it in SignNow: the button opens the closing form, with Elsie and Freddy already filled in as signers. You complete Sections 1–7 and sign; Elsie completes the file check (Section 8); Freddy signs to release (Section 10).</p><p><b>Submit within 2 business days of a signed contract.</b></p><p><b>Referral on the deal?</b> Send the Referral Agreement in SignNow first: Team Templates › GDC FORM - RA-4 - Referral Agreement - Rev 9-22 (Broker A is the referring brokerage, Broker B the receiving one). Then record the referral in Section 5 of the Contract to Closing form.</p>'+lnk(O.ccc,'Start it in SignNow')+'</div>'+'<div class="gp-box"><h3>Before commission is released</h3><ol><li>Executed contract and all addenda in SignNow</li><li>Listing or buyer brokerage agreement in the file; commission matches it</li><li>Brokerage relationship and wire-fraud disclosures signed</li><li>Escrow deposit receipt(s) on file</li><li>Referral agreement and W-9 attached (if a referral is paid)</li><li>Your onboarding package complete</li><li>Split, fee and amounts match your plan</li><li>Closing date and the closing form logged in the Deal Pipeline Tracker</li><li>Transaction task checklist complete</li></ol></div>'+'<div class="gp-box"><h3>Compliance log</h3><p>One row per transaction: package sent and signed, Contract to Closing submitted, the Managing Broker review (Waiting · Changes requested · Approved) and closing. Elsie keeps it; ask her for the status of your file.</p></div></div></section>';
  h+='<section class="gp-sec" id="dealroom"><h2>Internal deal room</h2><p class="gp-note"><b>Deals are not your listings.</b> “Deals” are the company\'s own developments and off-market opportunities, handled by the directors. Your listings and transactions are yours: start them in the Your work row and follow them under Submit a Transaction File › My files.</p><p class="gp-note">Company developments, data-center and off-market opportunities are confidential and live in the directors\' deal room, not on this page. If a client of yours fits one of them, ask A.J. or Elsie and the NDA goes out first.</p><p class="gp-note" style="margin-bottom:0"><a class="gp-btn gp-primary" href="mailto:aj.lash@goyaldecoster.com?cc=elsie.benitez@goyaldecoster.com&amp;subject=NDA%20request%20for%20a%20client&amp;body=Client%20name%3A%0ACompany%3A%0AClient%20email%3A%0AWhich%20deal%20or%20property%3A%0A">Request an NDA for a client</a></p><p class="gp-sn-n" style="margin:14px 0 0">How it works · for your information, nothing to click:</p><div class="gp-flow" style="margin-top:8px"><div class="gp-step"><b>1 · NDA on file</b><span>Before a client sees an OM or pro forma, our one-way NDA goes out through SignNow and the signed copy is filed. Ask A.J. or Elsie to send it.</span></div><div class="gp-step"><b>2 · Offering memorandum</b><span>Sent from the data room: watermarked, view-only, logged. Never email the PDF.</span></div><div class="gp-step"><b>3 · Pro forma</b><span>Released after the OM conversation, same room, same rules.</span></div><div class="gp-step"><b>Deal review · every other Tuesday</b><span>New inventory and status, 15-day cadence, on the GDC Directors calendar.</span></div></div>'+''+'</section>';
